  "result": "Done! I've implemented foreign currency support:\n\n**Added to src/money.js:**\n\n**RATES object:**\n- EUR: 1 (base currency)\n- USD: 1.085 (units of USD per euro)\n- GBP: 0.8425 (units of GBP per euro)\n\n**`convert(eurCents, currency)` function:**\n- Converts amount from EUR cents to target currency cents\n- Returns `ok(currencyCents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n- Formula: `currencyCents = roundCents(eurCents * RATES[currency])`\n- Supports EUR, USD, GBP\n\n**`formatMoney(cents, currency)` function:**\n- Formats currency amounts with proper symbol\n- EUR: \u20ac1,234.56\n- USD: $1,234.56\n- GBP: \u00a31,234.56\n- 2 decimal places\n- Thousands separators (commas)\n- Handles negative amounts with minus sign\n- Unknown currencies default to EUR formatting\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Added UNKNOWN_CURRENCY error code to errors.js\n\n**Added 21 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- RATES validation\n- EUR to EUR (identity)\n- EUR to USD conversion\n- EUR to GBP conversion\n- Unknown currency handling\n- Small, large, negative, and zero amounts\n- Rounding precision\n- formatMoney for all currencies\n- Negative amounts formatting\n- Thousands separator formatting\n- Unknown currency fallback\n\nAll 290 tests pass \u2713 (269 existing + 21 new currency tests)",
